# Cursor agent rules — Portafolio Yamir Rojo

Read `CURSOR_CONTEXT.md` first. It is the authoritative working brief for this repo.

## Hard rules

- Source of truth for site copy is `CV YAMIR MOISÉS ROJO ANDRADE MAESTRO.pdf`. The Maestro PDF is **never** published, linked, or copied to `public/`.
- Only `public/documents/cv-yamir-moises-rojo-andrade.pdf` (the Ejecutivo CV; download name `CV Yamir Moisés Rojo Andrade.pdf`) is exposed to visitors.
- **Do not invent** company names, metrics, dates, certifications, or recognitions. If a claim is not in one of the two PDFs, do not write it.
- `PLAN-PORTAFOLIO-YAMIR-ROJO-ANDRADE.md` is reference only — **do not edit it**. Current code has intentionally diverged (see §8 of `CURSOR_CONTEXT.md`).
- Bilingual content: `src/content/es.ts` and `src/content/en.ts` arrays are index-aligned. When you add, remove, or reorder an item in one language, mirror it in the other in the same operation.
- Light theme is class-name-driven via `globals.css` overrides. Any new `text-white/X`, `bg-white/X`, `bg-navy-*/X`, or `border-white/X` utility requires a matching `html[data-theme="light"]` override or contrast will break in day mode.
- Images must stay **static** on scroll. No parallax, no `whileInView` motion on figures. Hero portrait fade between photos is the only image animation allowed.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`: any new animation must opt out via the existing helpers.

## Stack invariants

- Astro 5 + React 18 islands (`client:load` for above-the-fold, `client:visible` otherwise).
- Tailwind 3 with `applyBaseStyles: false`; component classes live in `src/styles/globals.css` `@layer components`.
- TypeScript strict. Types for content live in `src/content/types.ts`.
- `motion` is installed but used sparingly (hero only). Don’t spread it across the codebase.

## Conventions

- Spanish copy first, English mirrors it faithfully (no marketing fluff added).
- Color tokens: `navy-950/900` (dark surfaces), `gold-400/500/600` (primary accent / active), `exec-blue` (secondary / index style), `exec-green` (availability / in-progress), plus `#3bbfd1` and `#e08a4f` for the 5-color block-identity palette on Tools/Certifications.
- Educación Básica uses `status: 'completed'` only — never `titled`, never “máxima distinción”.
- `Tools.astro` and `Certifications.astro` render grids of fully-visible cards. The React files are named `*Accordion.tsx` for historical reasons; do not reintroduce real accordion behavior there.
- Header lang/theme toggles are single buttons with icon + current-state word. Don’t replace them with wide segmented controls (they overlap the nav).
- CV is its own section (`Cv.astro`) with an inline `<iframe>`. Don’t reintroduce the legacy modal `CvViewer.tsx`.

## When in doubt

If user intent conflicts with the plan or with the current code, ask the user. Do not silently revert. Prefer minimal, additive changes that preserve existing patterns.

Update `CURSOR_CONTEXT.md` whenever architecture or conventions shift.
